Subject: [PATCH] Backport upstream postfix_internal_origin to Postfix 3.11.7

Upstream: Wietse Venema, postfix-3.12-20260915 (2026-09-15)
Announcement: https://www.mail-archive.com/postfix-devel@postfix.org/msg01355.html
Source archive: postfix-3.12-20260915.tar.gz
Source SHA256: b72082fcbaf36dae65ce7220e619200c50171920810a36ab79defa94ff8068fa
Target archive: postfix-3.11.7.tar.gz
Target SHA256: a2f3242345753448072177fae83c322a403c9263696996406201145dab8e8625

Backport prepared by Christian Roessner's RNS docker-postfix project.
The origin implementation, flags, source-class mapping, macro evaluation,
test input/output and provenance documentation are copied from the final
upstream snapshot. Upstream authorship and license notices are retained.
No legacy postfix_dsn_origin macro or downstream origin semantics remain.

Mechanical adaptations to the 3.11.7 baseline:
- Register cleanup_org_flag.c/.o in the existing global Makefile lists and
  retain the existing 3.11 test/build framework and unrelated dependencies.
- Add only postfix_internal_origin to the CONNECT default, without the
  unrelated 3.12 client_connections default addition.
- Add only the origin test/command, macro entry and documentation blocks;
  retain the existing TLS, UXTEXT and other unrelated 3.11 code/docs.
The upstream documentation's >= 3.12 statement is intentionally preserved:
this file is an explicitly identified downstream backport to 3.11.7.

Apply after postfix-3.11.7-sasl-external-client-cert.patch, without either
of the superseded postfix-3.11.7-dsn-origin patches.

